# {{.Type}}: {{.Name}}

`{{.Name}}` describes all private endpoint connection strings for one MongoDB Atlas cluster. It returns both `SELF_MANAGED` connection strings that the resource manages and read-only `IMPORTED` records that Atlas created when the project opted in. Optionally filter the results by `status` (`PENDING`, `AVAILABLE`, or `FAILED`) and `management_type` (`SELF_MANAGED` or `IMPORTED`).

~> **NOTE:** The Atlas API for this data source is in preview and can change before it becomes generally available. Your project must be opted in to private endpoint connection strings through the project setting `isPrivateEndpointConnectionStringsEnabled`. To use this data source, the requesting Service Account or API Key must have the Project Read Only role.

